 don't know what happens if children get  sick with both viruses  at the same time we don't have data to  speak to it  but i would presume and assume and worry  unfortunately  that children are co-infected by both  covid19 and influenza  likely will have a worse outcome than  children infected by  either them individually the flu is also  particularly dangerous for seniors  provinces are still working out how best  to distribute this year's vaccine  alberta and ontario plan to distribute  the high-dose formula  to long-term care residents who were at  the highest risk  but the vaccine won't be available in  canada for another month  and with covet 19 cases on the rise it's  difficult to know what the situation  across the country will be  once flu season finally arrives heather  urex west global news  calgary freedom with love up next a  couple's whirlwind fight for justice  this next story is a bit of an antidote  to all the bad news these days  it's about a professional athlete a  basketball star who put her career on  hold to embark on a journey for justice  maya moore took up the case of a man she  believed was wrongfully convicted  and as robin gill reports her journey  turned into a love story  i'm maya moore and i'm jonathan irons  for 13 years maya moore and jonathan  irons have been considered a team  well now they've put a ring on it we got  married a couple months ago and  we're we're excited to uh to just  continue this new chapter of life  together on abc's good morning america  the couple announced they tied the knot  two months ago a few years ago you know  we  acknowledged both acknowledged that we  had really strong feelings for each  other so much so that  you know i i wanted to marry her but at  the same time protect her because  being in a relationship with a man in  prison is  extremely difficult and painful moore  first developed a friendship with irons  when she was 18.  they met through a prison ministry he  was serving a 50-year sentence for  assault and burglary  moore who went on to have a career in  the women's nba began  advocating for changes to policing and  the legal system  in 2019 she decided to take a leave of  absence from the wnba  to help irons be vacated a year later  a judge overturned his conviction citing  a fingerprint at the crime scene that  was never produced as evidence  it could have saved him the 23 years he  spent in jail  [Applause]  i feel like i can live life now man i'm  free  moore hasn't played ball in almost two  years and she isn't in a rush to go back  to the court  right now i am trying to really just  breathe from this  long long battle her fight for social  justice isn't over  but for now it's time to reflect on a  story about liberty  and love robin gill global news  and that is global national for this  wednesday i'm donna friesen tonight's  your canada is a bird's eye view of the  sunset over surrey bc  we'd love to see your canada please  email it to viewers at  globalnational.com  thanks for watching i hope to see you  here again tomorrow take care of  yourselves  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  bye-bye
 

